  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Friday...\n\nShowers and thunderstorms will impact the region today. Storms \nwill begin over the western high terrain before moving northeast \nacross the region. The environment looks like a high shear low \nCAPE day with shear values in the 40-60 kt range and CAPE \ngenerally in the 500-1,000 J/kg range. Convection is expected to \nlast well into the night due to CAPE values remaining elevated \novernight and a strong 30-40 kt low level jet. The Storm \nPrediction Center has issued a risk level 1 of 5 for severe storms\neast of Billings with the potential for hail >1 inch and wind \ngusts >60 mph. PWAT values of 1-1.25 inches and long skinny CAPE \nprofiles will also be favorable for heavy rain, though storm \nmotions will be fast helping to limit flooding. Due to the \npotential for heavy rain, the Weather Prediction Center has issued\na level 1 of 4 risk for excessive rainfall for eastern Montana.\n\nSaturday will bring an additional round of showers and\nthunderstorms. Cooler temperatures in the low to mid levels and \ndewpoints near 60 F will help to unlock more CAPE Saturday with\nvalues potentially getting into the 1-2,000 J/kg range near the\nDakotas border with continued high shear. These atmospheric\nprofiles will lead to an increased large hail risk along with\nstrong winds. For these reasons the Storm Prediction Center has\nissued a level 2 of 5 risk for severe storms Saturday. Continued\nPWAT values above 1 inch will lead to a heavy rain threat with the\nWeather Prediction Center having issued a level 1 of 4 risk for\nexcessive rainfall Saturday for eastern Montana. \n\nThe chance for showers and especially thunderstorms has increased\nfor Sunday as soundings indicate more instability to go along with\nstrong shear. It is too early to know the potential severity of\nthese storms at this time. Monday will see continued precipitation\nchances (30-60%) with the threat for thunderstorms being \nsignificantly reduced. \n\nTemperatures will be in the 80s F today before cooling down into\nthe 70s F in the west Saturday. Sunday and Monday are expected to\nhave temperatures in the 70s F. Tuesday through Friday will see a\nwarmer and drier pattern take hold as an upper level Pacific \ntrough is expected to set up to far to our west to bring \nprecipitation chances. Temperatures are expected to increase into \nthe 80s and potentially 90s F Wednesday through Thursday. \nTorgerson",
